# Expired and FSBO intake (Matt 2026-10-05)

A CMA is built when we hold a sendable owner email, or a cell number we can text. No CRM person and no CMA for a home that is back on the market, or for an owner we can neither email nor text.

Run these checks before `createCmaRequest` and before the CRM person is created, in this order:

1. Live status. Skip Active, Pending, Coming Soon, and Closed after the expiry. Match the same address or the same parcel or taxlot. An unreadable listings probe does not create a person or a CMA. Retry on the next run.
2. Compliance. Skip a litigator and a deceased owner. The litigator tag is applied only when the skip-trace says the person is a litigator. TCPA-only and a DNC phone block calls and texts. They do not block email and they do not set `compliance:hard-stop`.
3. Email. A valid, non-suppressed owner email builds the CMA. The send stays email.
4. Cell. With no sendable email, a non-DNC number whose line type is mobile, wireless, or cell builds the CMA. The send is SMS, through the existing prospect SMS intro, after the letter is approved. Intake does not text. A landline, a VOIP number, or a phone with no line type does not build. A suppressed email is not used. A clean cell still builds.

The same checks gate FSBO intake, including a contact copied off the listing page. An untyped page phone is not a cell. Do not invent a line type or a litigator tag for a page contact.

Do not put this gate in `sendCmaToLead` or `createCmaRequest`. Those also serve inbound seller and lead-form CMAs.

The source of truth is `expired_listings.compliance_hard_stop` and `compliance_flags`, and the same columns on `fsbo_listings`. Write them at intake. Every expired and FSBO send path reads them. A litigator or deceased owner sets the column so the send stays blocked. A clean cell must not be tagged do-not-text because some other number was DNC.

When BatchData returns no email, try Tracerfy and then Apify before giving up. Keep the county record. Keep the fallback phone's line type. A fallback cell is a reason to build. A fallback landline is not.

This does not loosen CMA rules 1–23. Rule 6 still says do not build or send a home that is listed again. This rule is the intake-front version of that check. Nothing texts an owner from intake.
